jess_customer: Hey team — my tool call keeps returning 400 'invalid JSON' when I pass tool args. Repro below. Ticket INC-8421

sam_support: Thanks Jess. Can you paste the exact body you sent and the curl/SDK you used?

jess_customer: Using hosted API POST /v1/call. Body I sent (copied from client): ```{
  'tool': 'save_file',
  'args': {
    'path': '/tmp/data.txt',
    'content': 'Hello\uZZZZ world',
  },
}``` Response: 400 {"error":"Malformed tool args: invalid escape"}

sam_support: I see multiple issues: single quotes around keys (JSON requires double quotes), trailing comma after args, and `\\uZZZZ` is an invalid unicode escape (Z not a hex digit). Can you try with valid JSON: ```{
  "tool": "save_file",
  "args": {
    "path": "/tmp/data.txt",
    "content": "Hello world"
  }
}```

jess_customer: Tried that exact JSON and still get 400. I also tried escaping the backslash in the client: ```curl -X POST https://api.redwood.ai/v1/call -H 'Authorization: Bearer ...' -H 'Content-Type: application/json' -d '{"tool":"save_file","args":{"path":"/tmp/data.txt","content":"Hello\\\\uZZZZ world"}}'``` — same error.

mike_oncall: Escalating — I reproduced locally with a tiny node script. Our parser error: ```parser.go:142 parseEscape: invalid unicode escape '\uZZZZ' at offset 36```

lena_engineer: Quick triage: JSON spec allows `\\u` followed by four hex digits [0-9A-Fa-f]. 'Z' is invalid here, so parsers should reject it with a clear message. But the weird part: our sanitizer is folding unknown escapes into a placeholder which later breaks schema validation instead of surfacing the exact escape problem. That's causing confusing 400s.

sam_support: So root cause is malformed args (invalid unicode escape) compounded by our error bubble-up. Workarounds for customers are: remove the bad escape, supply a valid \uXXXX, or base64 the content field.

jess_customer: Removing the `\\uZZZZ` from the content field fixed it, thanks. But please improve error message so customers know it's an invalid `\\u` escape.

ticketbot: Ticket INC-8421 updated -> Escalated to ENG. Priority: P2.

lena_engineer: I'll open a PR to change the sanitizer to fail-fast on invalid escapes with a descriptive error ("invalid unicode escape at offset X") and add a unit test and regression. ETA ~48h.

mike_oncall: Logged follow-up to devops to check if any other ingestion paths normalize escapes oddly.

sam_support: I sent Jess a note with the workaround (remove escape or base64). Keeping ticket open until PR merges. :thumbsup:

jess_customer: Appreciated, that solved my immediate issue. Please CC me on the PR.

